(a) induction theorems as data: derive in a theory, or memorise (adopt as a ground axiom)?
    D = bits of the checked derivation; c = one-line citation in the theory with theta added;
    beta* = (D - c)/|theta| bits per symbol: memorising at the first occurrence is cheaper iff the axiom prior
    per symbol is below beta* (the track uses LAM = 4.52).
