(b) lemma reuse: commutativity with its two lemmas derived in-line, or cited after adopting them as axioms
    comm in T_Ind, lemmas in-line:   55 lines,  1358.6 bits
    comm in T_Ind + {add0l, addSl}:   23 lines,   504.7 bits   (saving 853.9 bits per use; the two lemmas cost 90.5 bits of prior)
    so the lemmas are adopted as axioms once comm (or anything using them) occurs 1 time(s).

(c) compressible theorems: instances of a schema form with large motives (seed 41)
    datum f(phi), phi a random motive with x free; per-datum bits under three hypotheses:
      derive  = bits of the schematic derivation of f(P) in T_Ind (c1_costs.py) + LAM*|phi| (L1-sch)
      memo    = LAM*|f(phi)| + citation           (adopt the datum itself as a ground axiom)
      templ   = citation + LAM*|phi|, plus LAM*|f(P)| of prior once (adopt the template f(P))
      Ind |phi| =  29  |f(phi)| =  127   derive   137.7   memo   581.0   templ   137.7 (+72 once)   cheapest per datum: derive (= cite Ind)
      Ind |phi| =  21  |f(phi)| =   94   derive   101.5   memo   431.7   templ   101.5 (+72 once)   cheapest per datum: derive (= cite Ind)
      Ind |phi| = 109  |f(phi)| =  458   derive   499.6   memo  2078.3   templ   499.6 (+72 once)   cheapest per datum: derive (= cite Ind)
      Ind |phi| = 429  |f(phi)| = 1779   derive  1947.1   memo  8053.9   templ  1947.1 (+72 once)   cheapest per datum: derive (= cite Ind)
      CVI |phi| =  19  |f(phi)| =   69   derive  1560.5   memo   318.6   templ    92.4 (+81 once)   cheapest per datum: memo
      CVI |phi| =  20  |f(phi)| =   72   derive  1565.0   memo   332.2   templ    97.0 (+81 once)   cheapest per datum: memo
      CVI |phi| = 123  |f(phi)| =  381   derive  2030.9   memo  1730.0   templ   562.9 (+81 once)   cheapest per datum: memo
      CVI |phi| = 418  |f(phi)| = 1266   derive  3365.4   memo  5733.3   templ  1897.3 (+81 once)   cheapest per datum: derive
      LNP |phi| =   7  |f(phi)| =   34   derive  2272.2   memo   160.3   templ    38.2 (+86 once)   cheapest per datum: memo
      LNP |phi| =  21  |f(phi)| =   76   derive  2335.5   memo   350.3   templ   101.5 (+86 once)   cheapest per datum: memo
      LNP |phi| = 104  |f(phi)| =  325   derive  2711.0   memo  1476.6   templ   476.9 (+86 once)   cheapest per datum: memo
      LNP |phi| = 400  |f(phi)| = 1213   derive  4050.0   memo  5493.6   templ  1815.9 (+86 once)   cheapest per datum: derive
    Ind(phi) in T_Ind is a citation, so "derive" is the template row: the schema compresses its instances by a
    factor of about |Ind(phi)|/|phi|.  For a non-primitive form (CVI, LNP in T_Ind) deriving beats memorising
    only when the motive is long; adopting the template beats both after one or two uses.

